# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 to dependencies
- Ran `npm install` to update node_modules and package-lock.json

### 2. Modified Files

#### `package.json`
- Added `@vercel/analytics: ^2.0.1` to dependencies

#### `package-lock.json`
- Updated with @vercel/analytics and its 93 transitive dependencies
- All dependencies resolved successfully with no vulnerabilities

#### `src/App.jsx`
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the root level (inside the main div, after the Footer component)

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics quickstart documentation:
- Fetched latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Used React-specific integration with `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Placed the Analytics component at the root level of the application for site-wide tracking
- No additional configuration required for Vite projects

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- No build errors or warnings
- All 476 modules transformed correctly
- Output bundle generated successfully (639.43 kB)

✅ No linter configured in project (skipped)
✅ No tests configured in project (skipped)

## Next Steps

To enable analytics:
1. Visit your Vercel dashboard's Analytics section
2. Click the "Enable" button for Web Analytics
3. Deploy this application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
4. Analytics will start tracking page views automatically

The Analytics component will automatically begin collecting page view data once deployed to Vercel and enabled in the dashboard.
